[resource]
script = ExtResource("1")
title = "Wildlife"
brief_tooltip = "Polar bears patrol the ice and attack intruders.
Wounded animals may flee.
Killed animals drop meat and pelts."
implemented = true
detailed_text = "[b]The Arctic Is Not Empty[/b]

[i]Inuit hunters knew the polar bear as Nanuq — lord of the ice. A full-grown male weighs half a ton, can outrun a man over short distances, and has been known to stalk human camps for days. The men of Franklin's expedition, weakened by scurvy and starvation, were no match for such a predator.[/i]

The island is home to dangerous wildlife. Polar bears are the greatest threat your men will face outside of the cold itself.

[b]Polar Bears[/b]

Polar bears are territorial. They patrol wide stretches of ice and coastline, and will investigate anything that enters their range.

• A bear that spots your men will approach to investigate
• If the intruders do not leave, the bear attacks
• Bears are powerful — a single bear can kill an unarmed man quickly
• Armed groups have a much better chance of driving one off

[b]After the Kill[/b]

A dead animal can be looted for meat and pelts. Bear meat feeds your crew; pelts may prove useful for warmth and crafting.

[b]Tips[/b]

• Never send a man alone into open ice — bears hunt the isolated
• Keep officers armed with hatchets when scouting
• A wounded bear may flee — do not assume the fight is over
• If a bear approaches your camp, order armed officers to intercept it before it reaches the men"
